# Trivy's ignore list for the weekly image scan (scripts/security/image-scan.sh, .github/workflows/image-scan.yml).
# Only a CRITICAL or HIGH with a fix fails the scan; one without a fix is shown and never listed here.
# Seeded from the triage of 2026-10-25 (docs/security/assessment.md, its CVE table): each entry is the id with the date
# Trivy stops ignoring it (exp:), then one comment line per image and package holding the verdict and the reason.
# Review every entry by its date: the scan fails again on it once the date has passed. One list serves every image, so
# an id ignored for one image is ignored for all; the comment names each image it was triaged for.
# A REACHABLE entry is here only because no fixed release of that image exists yet: take the release when it does.

CVE-2026-111497 exp:2026-11-25
#   HIGH caddy: brotli-libs — NOT REACHABLE: the caddy binary is static and links no brotli; libcurl alone pulls it in; fixed in Alpine, arrives with the tag's rebuild

CVE-2026-78669 exp:2026-11-25
#   HIGH caddy (the edge): Go stdlib, x/net — REACHABLE, DoS, LOW: HTTP/2 and range-request CPU floods on the only published port, no data exposed; no Caddy release carries Go 1.26.9 yet: move the edge when one does (assessment S7)
#   HIGH database, postgres: gosu's Go stdlib — NOT REACHABLE: gosu runs once at start, as root, to exec postgres, and opens no TLS, HTTP or network connection; fixed when the official postgres image is rebuilt on gosu 1.20

CVE-2026-111943 exp:2026-11-25
#   HIGH caddy: Go stdlib — NOT REACHABLE on a shop, LOW on a server: Caddy as a TLS client: ACME to the CA on a server only, and it needs a mis-issued intermediate; no fixed Caddy release
#   HIGH database, postgres: gosu's Go stdlib — NOT REACHABLE: gosu runs once at start, as root, to exec postgres, and opens no TLS, HTTP or network connection; fixed when the official postgres image is rebuilt on gosu 1.20

